# Half a second of cut while the host throws and the guest walks. Jump bound: a copy that
# comes back is placed and the render offset takes the move; the offset gives back at most
# 0.15 of 2 m a tick (0.3 m) and the body moves v dt = 6 m/s / 60 = 0.1 m on top: 0.45 m,
# derived; the same bound holds in the cut, hitch, rate and ping scenarios.
scenario cut_short
scene two_chars_item
seed 43
guests 1
settle 6s

net g1 rtt 100ms jitter 10ms loss 1%

p0 walk box
p0 grab box as lift
p0 wait 300ms
p0 throw 1.6 0.6 0.4 speed 6 as throw
p1 walk -1 -1 speed 2.5
p1 walk 1 1 as p1_back
at 1200ms cut g1 for 500ms

expect result lift granted
expect result throw done
expect agree_at_rest 5cm 5deg
expect no_stuck
expect jump.max <= 0.45m
# behind_ticks: a copy plays at most delay_max (15 ticks, before the clock knows the path)
# behind its owner's newest, plus the one-way delay and the jitter in ticks, plus 2 for the
# tick the packet arrives in and the tick the owner's newest is read after its step:
# 21, plus the 30-tick cut while nothing arrives: 51. Derived.
expect behind_ticks.max <= 51t
expect behind_ticks.p95 <= 51t
# lag_divergence.p95: measured (0.147 m), with a margin: a copy that holds its last snapshot or
# draws a stale moment reads several times that.
expect lag_divergence.p95 <= 0.25m
